course: dictionary
lesson: 11745
title: Confused and stuck
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Sometimes a puzzle has no answer you can see yet. Then you may feel baffled. Baffled means completely confused, so you cannot understand or explain something. The clues in the sentence show you the meaning.
explain: «The detective stared at the strange code, completely baffled.» The word completely shows how confused the detective is. Ask yourself: does the person understand, or are they stuck? Here they are stuck, so baffled must mean confused.
explain: «Mia was baffled when her answer was wrong, even after she checked it twice.» Baffled is not the same as angry or scared. It is the feeling of being stuck, with no clue how to fix the problem.
fact: Baffled means completely confused, and not able to understand or explain something.
fact: Baffle is a verb, so «The puzzle baffled the class» means the puzzle made the whole class confused.
fact: As an adjective, baffled describes a person: «She looked baffled.»
fact: Useful phrases: «completely baffled», «baffled by» something, and «left baffled».
fact: A good check is to swap in another word, such as «confused», and see if the sentence still makes sense.
exercise: «The detective read the note three times and was still baffled.» What does baffled mean here? | *Completely confused | Very happy | Bored and sleepy | Quick and clever
exercise: Lena says, «I am baffled by this science question.» What does she mean? | She is going to sing a song | *She cannot understand or explain the question | She has finished the question and got it right | She knows the answer already
exercise: Fill the gap with the best word: The puzzle ___ the whole class. | *baffled | hungry | sleepy | glowing
test: Ben stared at the broken clock, baffled. What does baffled mean? | Excited | *Completely confused | Hungry | Calm
test: Which sentence uses baffled correctly? | *The clues left the detective baffled. | The cake was baffled. | Baffled the sun is shining. | I was baffled, so I ran fast.
exam: Read: «Nobody could explain the ghost footprints, and the villagers were baffled.» Why were the villagers baffled? | *They could not understand or explain the footprints | They had won a prize at the fair | They were eating a big lunch | They were feeling very sleepy
